---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import meMemoji from "@assets/about/me-memoji.png";
import meHeadshot from "@assets/about/me-headshot.png";
import meAvatar from "@assets/about/me-avatar.png";
import meRainbow from "@assets/about/me-rainbow.png";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="about · thalida"
  activePage="about"
  pageContext={{ collection: "page", id: "about", title: "About" }}
>
  <article class="font-body max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="m-0 mb-2 font-display font-bold text-neon text-display-sm tracking-tighter leading-none">About</h2>
    <hr />

    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2 mb-6">
      <Image src={meMemoji} alt="A Memoji of Thalida" class="w-full h-auto border border-border rounded-lg" />
      <Image src={meHeadshot} alt="A headshot of Thalida" class="w-full h-auto border border-border rounded-lg" />
      <Image src={meAvatar} alt="A cartoon avatar of Thalida" class="w-full h-auto border border-border rounded-lg" />
      <Image
        src={meRainbow}
        alt="A rainbow themed image of Thalida"
        class="w-full h-auto border border-border rounded-lg"
      />
    </div>

    <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-teal mt-6 mb-2 tracking-tight">Hey, I'm Thalida!</h3>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      I'm a queer (pronouns they/she) first generation Trinidadian-American Engineer based in New York.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      Over 14 years ago for my 16th birthday I wanted one thing: a domain of my own. I was lucky enough to have a
      supportive mother who gifted me thalida.com, and over the years this site has been the place where I learn, grow,
      and experiment.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      I use this space to practice and learn, break things and experiment, grow and challenge myself in ways that have
      fewer consequences than messing around on a domain someone else owns. Here I am able to push myself as an
      engineer, designer, and writer. Which is all to say: if it's ever broken, janky, or weird, I'm probably in the
      process of learning something new, and you're coming along for the ride with me! ✨
    </p>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">If you're interested in connecting:</p>
    <ul class="text-text mb-4 pl-4 list-disc">
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/thalida/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
        <a href="https://github.com/thalida" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Github</a>
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed"><a href="mailto:hello@thalida.com">Email</a></li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-teal mt-6 mb-2 tracking-tight">Career History</h3>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      I have over 10 years of experience in the tech industry, working in various roles from Product Engineering to
      Engineering Management. My journey has taken me through startups, large corporations, and everything in between.
    </p>
    <ul class="text-text mb-4 pl-4 list-disc">
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">Currently, I'm an Engineering Manager at Zapier on the MCP Team!</li>
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
        Previously, I was Co-Founder and CTO of <a href="https://tourus.io">Tourus</a>, a VC-backed mobile-first AI,
        automation, and communication suite for property managers and leasing agents
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">
        Back in the day, I've worked at <a href="https://webflow.com/">Webflow</a>, <a href="https://www.etsy.com"
          >Etsy</a
        >, and <a href="https://www.okcupid.com/">OkCupid</a> as a Lead Engineer and Senior Engineering Manager
      </li>
      <li class="mb-2 leading-relaxed">I also have experience in design and product management</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-teal mt-6 mb-2 tracking-tight">About this site</h3>
    <p class="text-text mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      This site is built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and hosted on <a
        href="https://pages.cloudflare.com">Cloudflare Pages</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
